{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfieBkXkaJ9jeS9m6r6Bj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build phase is done: `@one-a-day/sports/cubing-average-card/v1` is built, with three variants, and variant c is left in place. `state.json` has `build: \"done\"`, `variants: [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]` and `inPlace: \"c\"`.\n\nThe build gate is clean, `npm test` passes (313 jest tests, 61 node tests), and every variant rendered with exit 0 and no error mosaic. I opened the square, landscape and portrait stills for all three variants and the tutorial pages 2 and 3 for c, and checked each claim against the picture. I also rendered a 12-solve stress card and a light-theme Mo3 to look at.\n\n- **a, bars from zero:** every claim is in the picture, but the five bars sit at 77–100% of the track and look alike.\n- **b, a tick at the average:** helps a little, but the bars still look alike.\n- **c, bars show distance from the average:**\n  - Left means faster and right slower, with the dropped solves hollow at the ends.\n  - It shows who carried the average and who dragged it, so it is the default.\n  - Length bars and the tick are one prop away.\n\nThe variants share the same code and differ only in their default props.\n\nThings the critic or tomorrow's agent may trip on, all written up in `30-build.md`:\n- The brief's 76% bar for solve 2 is actually 76.5%, which rounds to 77; the test pins 77.\n- Hollow bars are filled with the track colour, not the page colour the brief said, because the page colour reads as a cut-out.\n- The footnote wording for the +2 clause was changed after a and b were rendered, so their stills still show the old wording.\n- The cubing test takes about five minutes.\n\nScratch renders are under `journal/2026-10-04/scratch/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":22